  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}=\\hat{i}+2 \\hat{j}+3 \\hat{k}, \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{b}}=2 \\hat{i}+3 \\hat{j}-5 \\hat{k}$ and $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}}=3 \\hat{i}-\\hat{j}+\\lambda \\hat{k}$ be three vectors. Let $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{r}}$ be anit vector along $\\vec{b}+\\vec{c}$. If $\\vec{r} \\cdot \\vec{a}=3$, then $3 \\lambda$ is equal to:",
